--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SAMPLE TABLE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

[Fill in actual sample metadata before publishing. Column structure:]

Sample_ID | Condition | Outcome_Group | Sex | Age | Replicate | Batch
----------|-----------|---------------|-----|-----|-----------|------
...

Column definitions:
  Sample_ID     : Unique sample identifier
  Condition     : ICH (intracerebral hemorrhage) or Control
  Outcome_Group : Clinical outcome at 90 days; Good (mRS 0-3), Poor (mRS 4-6),
                  or NA for controls
  Sex           : M or F
  Age           : Age at sample collection (years)
  Replicate     : Biological replicate number within condition
  Batch         : Processing batch identifier

MTC groupings used in differential analyses:
  MTC_123 : Myeloid Trajectory Clusters 1, 2, 3 — associated with good outcome
  MTC_456 : Myeloid Trajectory Clusters 4, 5, 6 — associated with poor outcome


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FILE MANIFEST
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

File 0  : Overview.jpeg
Format  : JPEG image
Figures : N/A
Desc    : Graphical overview of the experimental design and analytical workflow.
          Shows the scRNA-seq pipeline from patient samples through myeloid
          subtype annotation, outcome-associated trajectory analysis, cell-cell
          interaction, drug repurposing, and in vivo validation.

File 1  : 1.Table_Dreamlet_DEGs_CellPop.csv
Format  : CSV
Figures : Figure 1E
Script  : Figures/Figure1/1.Figure1_E_Dreamlet.R
Desc    : Pseudobulk differential expression results (dreamlet/limma-voom)
          across major immune cell populations comparing ICH outcome groups.
          All tested genes included.

File 2  : 2.Table_Dreamlet_DEGs_Myeloids_logFC_1.5.csv
Format  : CSV
Figures : Figure 2D
Script  : Figures/Figure2/2.Figure2_D_CL_DEGs.R
Desc    : Dreamlet DE results for myeloid subpopulations filtered to
          |logFC| >= 1.5. Input for pathway and enrichment analyses.

File 3  : 3.Table_DEGs_MTC_456_vs_123_FULL_nonsig_incl_tstat.tsv
Format  : TSV (tab-separated)
Figures : Figure 2B-D
Script  : scripts/7.DEG_Metacells.R
Desc    : Complete DEG table comparing MTC_456 (poor outcome) versus MTC_123
          (good outcome) using metacell-level Wilcoxon statistics. Includes
          non-significant genes and t-statistics.

File 4  : 4.DE_Tfs_MTC.csv
Format  : CSV
Figures : Figure 2E
Script  : Figures/Figure2/2.Figure2_E_GRN.R
Desc    : Differential transcription factor activity between MTC groups,
          derived from pySCENIC regulon activity scores.

File 5  : 5.DE_CCI_MTC123_vs_MTC456.csv
Format  : CSV
Figures : Figure 3A-B
Scripts : Figures/Figure3/3.Figure3_A_Liana.py,
          Figures/Figure3/3.Figure3_B_CellChat.R
Desc    : Differential cell-cell interaction scores between MTC_123 and
          MTC_456, computed via LIANA and CellChat. Each row is a
          ligand-receptor pair in a sender-receiver cell-type context.

File 6a : 6a.IREA_MTC123.csv
Format  : CSV
Figures : Figure 3C
Script  : Figures/Figure3/3.Figure3_C_IREA.R
Desc    : IREA (Immune Response Enrichment Analysis) cytokine activity scores
          for MTC_123 (good outcome) clusters. Each row is a cytokine family
          with enrichment score and adjusted p-value.

File 6b : 6b.IREA_MTC456.csv
Format  : CSV
Figures : Figure 3C
Script  : Figures/Figure3/3.Figure3_C_IREA.R
Desc    : IREA cytokine activity scores for MTC_456 (poor outcome) clusters.
          Paired with 6a; both files are passed to the plotting script for
          side-by-side enrichment comparison.

File 7  : README
Format  : Plain text, no extension
Figures : N/A
Desc    : This file.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
COLUMN DEFINITIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

--- File 1: 1.Table_Dreamlet_DEGs_CellPop.csv ---

  assay        : Major immune cell type label (e.g., T Cells, MONO, Myeloid)
  ID           : Gene symbol (same as 'gene')
  gene         : HGNC gene symbol
  logFC        : Log2 fold change (ICH vs Control or Poor vs Good outcome)
  AveExpr      : Average log2 expression across all samples
  t            : Moderated t-statistic (dreamlet/limma)
  P.Value      : Nominal p-value
  adj.P.Val    : Benjamini-Hochberg FDR-adjusted p-value
  B            : Log-odds of differential expression (B-statistic)
  z.std        : Standardized z-score
  diffexpressed: Significance call: "UP", "DOWN", or "NS" (not significant)
  cluster      : Compound label combining outcome group and cell type
                 (e.g., "Good_T Cells")
  pos_avgLFC   : Positive-direction average logFC across cell types
  avg_LFC      : Average logFC across cell types


--- File 2: 2.Table_Dreamlet_DEGs_Myeloids_logFC_1.5.csv ---

  assay        : Myeloid subtype label (e.g., Adapt_AIF1, PVM_CD163)
  ID           : Gene symbol (same as 'gene')
  gene         : HGNC gene symbol
  logFC        : Log2 fold change
  AveExpr      : Average log2 expression across all samples
  t            : Moderated t-statistic
  P.Value      : Nominal p-value
  adj.P.Val    : Benjamini-Hochberg FDR-adjusted p-value
  B            : Log-odds of differential expression (B-statistic)
  z.std        : Standardized z-score
  pos_avgLFC   : Positive-direction average logFC across myeloid subtypes
  avg_LFC      : Average logFC across myeloid subtypes


--- File 3: 3.Table_DEGs_MTC_456_vs_123_FULL_nonsig_incl_tstat.tsv ---

  gene         : HGNC gene symbol
  p_val        : Nominal p-value (Wilcoxon rank-sum on metacells)
  p_val_adj    : Bonferroni-corrected p-value
  cluster      : MTC group with higher expression ("MTC_456" or "MTC_123")
  avg_log2FC.y : Log2 fold change (MTC_456 relative to MTC_123)
  pct.1.y      : Fraction of MTC_456 metacells expressing the gene
  pct.2.y      : Fraction of MTC_123 metacells expressing the gene
  sd.1         : Standard deviation of expression in MTC_456 metacells
  sd.2         : Standard deviation of expression in MTC_123 metacells
  RNA.MTC.123  : Mean expression in MTC_123 metacells
  RNA.MTC.456  : Mean expression in MTC_456 metacells
  se           : Standard error of the mean difference
  tstat        : t-statistic
  log2FC       : Log2 fold change (MTC_456 / MTC_123)


--- File 4: 4.DE_Tfs_MTC.csv ---

  gene         : Transcription factor symbol
  p_val        : Nominal p-value
  avg_log2FC   : Average log2 fold change of regulon activity (Poor vs Good)
  pct.1        : Fraction of cells in group 1 with detectable TF regulon
  pct.2        : Fraction of cells in group 2 with detectable TF regulon
  p_val_adj    : Adjusted p-value
  cluster      : MTC group label
  abs_avg_log2FC: Absolute value of avg_log2FC


--- File 5: 5.DE_CCI_MTC123_vs_MTC456.csv ---

  CCI          : Interaction label: sender_cell:ligand.receptor
  MTC_123      : Interaction score in MTC_123
  MTC_456      : Interaction score in MTC_456
  log2FC       : Log2 fold change (MTC_456 / MTC_123); negative = higher in 123
  cluster      : Group with higher interaction score
  Orientation  : Whether the MTC cells act as Senders or Receivers


--- Files 6a-6b: IREA_MTC123.csv / IREA_MTC456.csv ---

  Cytokine     : Cytokine or cytokine family name
  Enrichment.Score : IREA enrichment score for cytokine activity
  padj         : Benjamini-Hochberg adjusted p-value
  (Cond column added by plotting script: "MTC_123" or "MTC_456")


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
HOW TO LOAD THE DATA
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

--- Python ---

    import pandas as pd

    deg_cellpop = pd.read_csv("1.Table_Dreamlet_DEGs_CellPop.csv")

    deg_mtc_full = pd.read_csv(
        "3.Table_DEGs_MTC_456_vs_123_FULL_nonsig_incl_tstat.tsv",
        sep="\t"
    )

    irea_123 = pd.read_csv("6a.IREA_MTC123.csv")
    irea_456 = pd.read_csv("6b.IREA_MTC456.csv")

    sig = deg_cellpop[deg_cellpop["adj.P.Val"] < 0.05]


--- R ---

    deg_cellpop <- read.csv("1.Table_Dreamlet_DEGs_CellPop.csv",
                            stringsAsFactors = FALSE)

    deg_mtc_full <- read.delim(
        "3.Table_DEGs_MTC_456_vs_123_FULL_nonsig_incl_tstat.tsv",
        sep = "\t", stringsAsFactors = FALSE
    )

    irea_123 <- read.csv("6a.IREA_MTC123.csv", stringsAsFactors = FALSE)
    irea_456 <- read.csv("6b.IREA_MTC456.csv", stringsAsFactors = FALSE)

    sig <- subset(deg_cellpop, adj.P.Val < 0.05)

    # Reproduce Figure 3C:
    # Rscript Figures/Figure3/3.Figure3_C_IREA.R \
    #   6a.IREA_MTC123.csv 6b.IREA_MTC456.csv Figure3C.pdf


